      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:3:21:10",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) رَجُلٌ أَتَى رَجُلًا قَالَ عَلَيْهِ إِنْ كَانَ مُحْصَناً الْقَتْلُ وَ إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ مُحْصَناً فَعَلَيْهِ الْحَدُّ قَالَ قُلْتُ فَمَا عَلَى الْمُؤْتَى قَالَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَتْلُ عَلَى كُلِّ حَالٍ مُحْصَناً كَانَ أَوْ غَيْرَ مُحْصَنٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Al Husayn Bin Muhammad Al Ashary, from Moala Bin Muhammad, from Al Hassan Bin Ali, from Hammad Bin Usman who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘A man comes to a man’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Upon him, if he was married, is the killing, and if does not happen to be married, so upon him would be the Penalty (<span class=\"iTxt\">Hadd</span>)’. I said, ‘So what is upon the passive one?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Upon him is the killing, upon every state, be he married or without a marriage’."
        ]
      }
    },
